    "43": [
        "There are numerous UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Italy, including the Historic Centre of Florence, the Historic Centre of Rome, the City of Venice and its Lagoon, the Historic Centre of San Gimignano, the City of Vicenza and the Palladian Villas of the Veneto, the Archaeological Areas of Pompeii, Herculaneum and Torre Annunziata, the Amalfi Coast, the Historic Centre of Siena, the Historic Centre of Pienza, the Val d'Orcia, the Villa d'Este in Tivoli, the Late Baroque Towns of the Val di Noto, the Syracuse and the Rocky Necropolis of Pantalica, the Etruscan Necropolises of Cerveteri and Tarquinia, the Valcamonica rock art, the Longobards in Italy, the Rhaetian Railway, the Prehistoric Pile Dwellings around the Alps, the Medici Villas and Gardens, the Mount Etna, the Vineyard Landscape of Piedmont, the Arab-Norman Palermo and the Cathedral Churches of Cefalù and Monreale, the Ancient and Primeval Beech Forests of the Carpathians and the Ancient and Primeval Beech Forests of Germany, the Ivrea industrial city of the 20th century, the Prosecco Hills of Conegliano and Valdobbiadene, the Le Colline del Prosecco di Conegliano e Valdobbiadene, the Islands of the Gulf of Naples, the Historic Centre of Urbino, the Ferrara, City of the Renaissance, and the Po Delta."
    ],
